<title>USA: Calif. panel okays bonds for Mobil Corp - Treasurer.</title>
<headline>Calif. panel okays bonds for Mobil Corp - Treasurer.</headline>
<dateline>SACRAMENTO, Calif. 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>A California state panel has approved a $45 million tax-exempt bond issue to benefit Mobil Corp, state officials said Thursday.</p>
<p>The California Debt Limit Allocation Committee approved the bonds without debate. The bonds would be issued by the state to help the company fund facility improvements in California, state Treasurer Matt Fong's office said.</p>
<p>The state Pollution Control Financing Authority would issue the bonds, which would be repaid by the company. The bonds come from a $1.5 billion fund administered by the state to fund low-income housing, student loans, industrial developments and tax-exempt facilities.</p>
</text>
